<title>UK: Ontario sets 10 billion yen dual-currency bond.</title>
<headline>Ontario sets 10 billion yen dual-currency bond.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-03-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following bond was announced by lead manager Daiwa.</p>
<p> BORROWER   PROVINCE OF ONTARIO</p>
<p> AMT    10 BLN YEN    COUPON    *3.20 PCT  MATURITY    26.MAR.07</p>
<p> TYPE	 STRAIGHT  ISS PRICE  100.075   PAY DATE  S-03.APR.97</p>
<p> FULL FEES  32.50 BP  LISTING    NONE	PAY FREQ    ANNUAL</p>
<p> MOODY/S&amp;P  AA3/AA-   DENOMS (M) 100	 SALE LIMITS US/UK/JP</p>
<p> NEG PLG    NO	  CRS DEFLT  NO	  FORCE MAJ   YES</p>
<p> GOV LAW    ONTARIO   HOME CTRY  =	   TAX PROVS   GROSS UP</p>
<p> NOTES    S-SHORT FIRST COUPON</p>
<p>	     *COUPON IN A$, REDEMPTION IN YEN</p>
<p>		ISSUED OFF PROGRAMME FOR DEBT ISSUANCE</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7658</p>
</text>
